# Dr Brain - Mazes — LLM Guide

Dr Brain - Mazes (the second game in the Dr Brain collection) is a tower-maze puzzle for humans
and AI agents. A tower has one or more levels (floors); each level is a grid of round stone tiles
over a void. You walk one tile at a time from START (always on level 0, the bottom) to FINISH
(always on the top level), using stairs to change level and teleporting portal holes within a level. Reach FINISH
within the move limit to win. The tower is fogged: you only ever see the level you stand on.

Humans: open {{.BaseURL}}/ , pick a map and walk with the arrow keys. Tutorial: {{.BaseURL}}/learn
Spectate a session live: {{.BaseURL}}/watch/SESSION_ID

GraphQL endpoint:       POST {{.BaseURL}}/graphql
GraphQL subscriptions:  {{.WSURL}}/graphql  (graphql-ws protocol)
Playground:             GET  {{.BaseURL}}/playground
Introspection:          enabled unless the operator disabled it — query __schema/__type

Every example below is valid against the live schema. Replace SESSION_ID with an id returned by
createSession and MAP_ID with an id from the `maps` query.

---

## Rules

- A session is one game on one map. The map is snapshotted when the session is created.
- You move manually, one tile per move: UP, RIGHT, DOWN or LEFT. There is no program or timer.
- A position is `{ level, x, y }`. `level` 0 is the bottom floor; `x` is the column; `y` is the
  row, row 0 being the TOP row of a level (`y` grows DOWNWARD). UP = y-1, RIGHT = x+1,
  DOWN = y+1, LEFT = x-1. Moves never change the level by themselves.
- The start is always on level 0 and the finish always on the top level, so the goal level is
  `levelCount - 1`. Every level has the same width and height.

### Fog: you only see the level you stand on

- `maps` / `map` return the public catalog: `levelCount`, `width`, `height`, `maxMoves`,
  `parMoves`, `minLevelChanges`, `forcedDescents` and `preview` (the glyph rows of level 0,
  where every game starts). They never
  contain other levels, the finish position or portal twins. There is no whole-map query for
  players.
- A session carries `view`: `{ level, levelCount, rows, portals }` for the level you are on right
  now. Read it after every move; it changes when stairs take you to another level.
  `rows` is a list of row strings using these glyphs:

| glyph | tile                                                                              |
|-------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `.`   | void: not walkable                                                                |
| `o`   | stone: walkable                                                                   |
| `S`   | start: walkable, the only one, on level 0                                         |
| `F`   | finish: walkable, the only one, on the top level; stepping on it wins            |
| `U`   | stairs up: stepping on it lifts you to the SAME x,y on level+1                    |
| `D`   | stairs down: stepping on it drops you to the SAME x,y on level-1                  |
| `1`-`9` | portal hole: each digit appears exactly twice on the same level; stepping on one teleports you to its twin |

- `view.portals` lists the holes on the viewed level: `glyph`, `a` (the hole on this level) and
  `b` (its twin, always on this same level too).
- Stairs are paired: every `U` at level l (x,y) has a `D` at level l+1 (x,y) and vice versa.
  Stepping on a stairs tile takes you to the same x,y of the adjacent level and you LAND ON the
  matching arrow there (never on `S`, `F` or plain stone). Effects never chain: arriving on the
  paired stairs or on a portal's twin hole does not trigger it. To use it you step off and back
  on again, so wherever you can go up you can also go back down from the same x,y. A stairs tile
  can never be crossed as a corridor: stepping on it always takes it.
- A move into void or off the edge is BLOCKED: nothing happens and it is NOT counted
  (`lastEvent.blocked: true`). Every successful move counts, including stairs and portal moves.
- Win: stepping on `F`. Lose: `state.moves` reaches the map's `maxMoves` without winning
  (`lossReason: MOVE_LIMIT`). A win on the last allowed move still wins.
- `parMoves` is the shortest possible winning route (null if the finish is unreachable). Compare
  `state.moves` or `bestMoves` with it.
- `forcedDescents` is the fewest `D` stairs any winning route must take: 0 means you can climb
  straight up; more means some floor's way up is only reachable from below.
  `minLevelChanges` is the fewest stairs any winning route takes, always
  `levelCount - 1 + 2 * forcedDescents`. Both are null if the finish is unreachable.
- `status`: READY (no counted move yet), PLAYING, WON, LOST. WON/LOST sessions refuse further
  moves (`SESSION_TERMINAL`) until `reset`.
- `reset` puts you back on the start; `attempts` (finished games) and `bestMoves` (fewest moves
  in a won game, null before the first win) are kept.

### Move events

`lastEvent` describes the last attempt: `move` (counted-move index), `direction`, `from`,
`stepped` (tile entered), `to` (final tile after stairs/portal), `blocked`, `via`
(NONE, WALK, STAIRS_UP, STAIRS_DOWN, PORTAL), `status`, `lossReason`. A blocked attempt still
bumps the session `seq` so watchers see it. `state.path` lists every tile you entered, in order.

### Errors

Errors carry `extensions.code`: NOT_FOUND, SESSION_TERMINAL, INVALID_ARGUMENT, FORBIDDEN,
LIMIT_REACHED. Admin operations (map editing, `adminMap`) need an `X-Admin-Key` header and are not
for players. At most 20000 directions per
`bulkMove` call.

