## Quick start

1. List maps (public catalog, level 0 preview only):

```graphql
query { maps { id name difficulty width height levelCount preview maxMoves parMoves minLevelChanges forcedDescents } }
```

2. Create a session and read the level you start on:

```graphql
mutation { createSession(mapID: "MAP_ID", displayName: "my agent") { id state { pos { level x y } status } view { level levelCount rows portals { glyph a { level x y } b { level x y } } } map { maxMoves parMoves } } }
```

3. Move one tile at a time and read the new `view` (it changes level on stairs and portals):

```graphql
mutation { move(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", direction: RIGHT) { seq state { pos { level x y } moves status lossReason } view { level rows portals { glyph a { level x y } b { level x y } } } lastEvent { blocked via stepped { level x y } to { level x y } } } }
```

4. Or send several moves at once. It stops early once the game is WON or LOST, and at the first
   blocked move, so a wrong plan never keeps running from the wrong tile: look at
   `lastEvent.blocked` and `state.pos`, then send a corrected plan. Pass `stopOnBlocked: false` to
   skip blocked moves and carry on instead. `lastEvent` is the last attempt; you only get the
   final `view`:

```graphql
mutation { bulkMove(sessionID: "SESSION_ID", directions: [RIGHT, RIGHT, DOWN]) { state { pos { level x y } moves status } view { level rows } lastEvent { blocked direction } bestMoves attempts } }
```

5. Start over, or read / watch the session:

```graphql
mutation { reset(sessionID: "SESSION_ID") { state { status moves } view { level rows } attempts bestMoves } }
```

```graphql
query { session(id: "SESSION_ID") { seq attempts bestMoves view { level levelCount rows } state { pos { level x y } moves status lossReason path { level x y } } lastEvent { blocked via } } }
```

```graphql
subscription { sessionUpdated(sessionID: "SESSION_ID") { seq event { move direction blocked via } session { view { level rows } state { pos { level x y } moves status } } } }
```

The subscription emits the current snapshot immediately, then every change. Every update is a
full snapshot; ignore updates whose `seq` is not greater than the last one you saw.

Other session calls: `renameSession(id, displayName)`, `deleteSession(id)`. Query
`sessions(sort: RECENT, limit: 50, mapId: "...")` lists sessions.

---

## Tips

- Keep your own map of what you have seen: after each move store `view.rows` under
  `view.level`, and the portal ends you have used. Levels you have not visited are unknown.
- Explore with a search over states `(level, x, y)`: a neighbour is reached by one move; if the
  tile entered is `U`, `D` or a portal hole, the state after the move is the landing tile (same
  x,y one level up/down, or the twin hole, whose location `view.portals` already gives you).
- Head for the top level (`levelCount - 1`): the finish is there. A `U` tile on the level you are
  on leads one level up at the same x,y, where you land on a `D`; step off and on to come back.
- Void tiles and the map edge are free walls: probing them costs nothing (but they do appear as
  blocked events).
- After stairs or a portal, `state.pos` is the landing tile (the paired arrow or the twin hole)
  and you may leave it in any direction without bouncing back; `state.path` records both the
  tile you stepped on and the landing tile.
- `parMoves` is the minimum, so matching it is an optimal run.
